&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Presque tous ceux qui disent « l'upscale IA a empiré ma vidéo » ont raison sur le symptôme et tort sur le coupable. Ils ont passé un clip 360p dans un modèle 4×, obtenu un fichier 1440p au rendu plastique, et conclu que l'upscale est une arnaque.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Ce n'est pas le cas. Ce qui s'est passé, c'est qu'ils ont appliqué &lt;strong&gt;un seul&lt;/strong&gt; modèle de restauration à un contenu qui en nécessitait &lt;strong&gt;quatre&lt;/strong&gt; différents. Une sortie 4K n'est pas un produit ; c'est le dernier maillon d'une chaîne, et chaque preset de cette chaîne optimise pour un type de dégradation différent.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Cet article détaille les cinq presets que j'utilise le plus, ce que chacun fait réellement au niveau du pixel, et les règles de décision pour savoir lequel choisir. Si vous ne lisez qu'une chose, sautez au tableau final — mais le raisonnement compte plus que le tableau, parce que les presets interagissent.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  L'erreur : traiter l'upscale comme une opération unique
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Un upscaler neuronal fait deux choses à la fois :&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Reconstruction&lt;/strong&gt; — invente un détail plausible là où la source n'en a pas (bords, texture, mèches de cheveux).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Restauration&lt;/strong&gt; — retire les artefacts que la compression précédente a déjà cuits (blocs, ringing, banding, bruit de moustique).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Ces deux tâches se combattent. Si vous poussez fort la reconstruction sur une source pleine de blocs JPEG, le modèle affine ces blocs avec assurance jusqu'à en faire de petits rectangles nets. C'est le phénomène du « c'est pire après upscale », et c'est une erreur de choix de modèle, pas un problème de 4K.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;La vraie question n'est donc jamais &lt;em&gt;« quel est le meilleur upscaler ? »&lt;/em&gt; mais &lt;strong&gt;« quel type de dégradation ce fichier précis a-t-il, et quel modèle est le moins susceptible de l'amplifier ? »&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Ce que chaque preset optimise réellement
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Voici les cinq que je garde en rotation, avec une description honnête du compromis de chacun. Tous les exemples sont le même sujet, la même résolution source et le même facteur d'échelle — seul le preset change.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Natural HD — la valeur sûre
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Ffiles.catbox.moe%2F1k5ox3.jpg" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Ffiles.catbox.moe%2F1k5ox3.jpg" alt="Preset Natural HD : comparaison avant/après sur un portrait, source douce à gauche, détail résolu à droite" width="" height=""&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;C'est le preset qui s'efforce le plus de &lt;strong&gt;ne pas&lt;/strong&gt; paraître traité par IA. Il reconstruit le minimum de détail nécessaire pour que l'image se lise comme nette à distance normale de visionnage, puis s'arrête.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Fort en :&lt;/strong&gt; quasiment aucun artefact de halo, la peau reste couleur peau au lieu de devenir cireuse, le texte reste lisible.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Faible en :&lt;/strong&gt; il refuse d'inventer des mèches de cheveux ou la trame d'un tissu que la source a réellement perdu. Si vous avez besoin d'un détail médico-légal, il sous-livre exprès.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;À utiliser pour :&lt;/strong&gt; tout ce où le réalisme compte plus que la netteté — portraits, photos produit, immobilier, interviews, photos de famille.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Si vous ne devez utiliser qu'un seul preset dans votre vie, prenez celui-ci. &lt;strong&gt;Il échoue avec élégance&lt;/strong&gt;, ce que presque aucun modèle ne peut dire.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Ultra Crisp — pour un contenu net à l'origine mais devenu mou
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Ffiles.catbox.moe%2Fy8lxqy.jpg" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Ffiles.catbox.moe%2Fy8lxqy.jpg" alt="Preset Ultra Crisp : portrait cosplay steampunk, bords et ferrures métalliques résolus après upscale" width="" height=""&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Ultra Crisp suppose que la source a des bords propres qui ont seulement été floutés, pas détruits. Il pousse agressivement le contraste des bords.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Fort en :&lt;/strong&gt; graphismes, illustrations, produit sur fond blanc, captures d'UI, détail de cosplay et de costume, tout ce qui a des frontières dures entre sujet et fond.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Faible en :&lt;/strong&gt; sur des sources bruitées ou très compressées, il affine aussi le bruit. Des halos apparaissent sur les bords à fort contraste. La peau peut devenir rude.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;À utiliser pour :&lt;/strong&gt; un contenu qui a été &lt;strong&gt;réduit&lt;/strong&gt; plutôt que &lt;strong&gt;mal encodé&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;La distinction compte : &lt;strong&gt;réduit&lt;/strong&gt; signifie que le détail a été moyenné et peut être partiellement récupéré. &lt;strong&gt;Mal encodé&lt;/strong&gt; signifie que le détail a été remplacé par des artefacts de compression, et un affûtage fort ne fait que rendre ces artefacts plus bruyants.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  True Texture — reconstruire tissu et matière
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Ffiles.catbox.moe%2Fyom6ix.jpg" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Ffiles.catbox.moe%2Fyom6ix.jpg" alt="Preset True Texture : manteau d'hiver et bordure en fausse fourrure, texture de la matière récupérée sur la moitié droite" width="" height=""&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;True Texture est réglé pour les surfaces de matière : maille, fourrure, denim, cuir, veinage du bois, cheveux. Il privilégie une micro-texture plausible plutôt que la netteté des bords.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Fort en :&lt;/strong&gt; les vêtements et surfaces cessent de ressembler à du plastique peint. La fourrure et la maille se lisent correctement à 100 % de zoom.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Faible en :&lt;/strong&gt; il peut inventer une texture qui n'a jamais existé, ce qui pose problème si vous avez besoin d'exactitude (médical, archives, preuve documentaire). Il est aussi plus lent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;À utiliser pour :&lt;/strong&gt; mode, portraits avec détail vestimentaire visible, restauration de photos anciennes où vous voulez que la matière semble réelle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Ce qu'il faut comprendre de True Texture : c'est le preset &lt;strong&gt;le plus disposé à halluciner&lt;/strong&gt;. C'est un atout pour l'image commerciale et un passif pour tout ce qui est probatoire.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Cinema Vivid — couleur et contraste, pas résolution
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Ffiles.catbox.moe%2Fccu1ds.jpg" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Ffiles.catbox.moe%2Fccu1ds.jpg" alt="Preset Cinema Vivid : illustration animée, moitié gauche terne contre moitié droite saturée et à fort contraste" width="" height=""&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Cinema Vivid ne touche presque pas à la résolution. Ce qu'il change, c'est le mappage tonal — saturation, contraste local, point noir.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Fort en :&lt;/strong&gt; une matière plate, terne, type log ou mal étalonnée reprend vie. Fonctionne bien sur l'animation et le contenu stylisé où la séparation des couleurs est le sujet.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Faible en :&lt;/strong&gt; il poussera une source déjà saturée jusqu'à l'écrêtage. Les tons de peau dérivent vers l'orange. &lt;strong&gt;Ce n'est pas du tout un preset de restauration.&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;À utiliser pour :&lt;/strong&gt; contenu social, animation, vignettes — tout ce où l'&lt;em&gt;impact&lt;/em&gt; l'emporte sur l'&lt;em&gt;exactitude&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Soyez honnête avec celui-ci. C'est un étalonnage couleur déguisé en upscaler. C'est très bien, tant que vous le savez.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Clear Reality — le polyvalent pour les dégradations du monde réel
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Ffiles.catbox.moe%2F09rq4n.jpg" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Ffiles.catbox.moe%2F09rq4n.jpg" alt="Preset Clear Reality : portrait en extérieur, structure du fond flou résolue tandis que le sujet reste naturel" width="" height=""&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Clear Reality tente d'équilibrer reconstruction et suppression des artefacts. C'est celui que j'utilise quand je &lt;strong&gt;ne connais pas l'historique de la source&lt;/strong&gt; — vidéo de téléphone d'origine inconnue, clips téléchargés, capture de capture.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Fort en :&lt;/strong&gt; gère une dégradation mixte (un peu de flou, un peu de compression, un peu de bruit) sans échec spectaculaire dans aucune direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Faible en :&lt;/strong&gt; c'est l'option de compromis, donc il est rarement le &lt;em&gt;meilleur&lt;/em&gt; sur un point isolé. Sur une source propre, Ultra Crisp gagne. Sur du tissu, True Texture gagne.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;À utiliser pour :&lt;/strong&gt; des séquences hétérogènes du monde réel où vous ne pouvez pas inspecter chaque image.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Pourquoi l'ordre compte plus que le preset
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;C'est la partie que presque tous les tutoriels sautent. &lt;strong&gt;Le choix du preset est la deuxième décision. La première, c'est ce qui se passe avant que l'upscaler tourne.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Si votre source a des blocs visibles ou du bruit de moustique, appliquez une passe de débruitage &lt;strong&gt;d'abord&lt;/strong&gt;. Si vous upscalez d'abord et débruitez ensuite, l'upscaler a déjà amplifié les artefacts en détail à fort contraste, et le débruiteur doit maintenant se battre contre la sortie de son propre modèle. Vous perdez deux fois.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;L'ordre pratique qui fonctionne :&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Inspectez&lt;/strong&gt; à 200–400 % de zoom. Identifiez la dégradation dominante : flou, blocs, bruit ou banding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Débruitez&lt;/strong&gt; s'il y a des blocs ou du bruit. Touche légère — vous voulez retirer les artefacts, pas le détail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Corrigez couleur/exposition&lt;/strong&gt; avant l'upscale, pas après. Upscaler une image surexposée cuit l'écrêtage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Upscalez&lt;/strong&gt; avec le preset adapté au &lt;em&gt;type de contenu&lt;/em&gt; (tableau ci-dessous).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Affûtez en dernier&lt;/strong&gt;, et doucement. Un léger masque flou après upscale récupère une netteté perçue sans réintroduire de halos.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Tableau de décision
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;État de la source&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Preset&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Pourquoi&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Propre mais petite (réduite)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Ultra Crisp&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Bords intacts, juste moyennés — récupérables&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Blocs / bruit de moustique&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Débruitage → Clear Reality&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Supprimer les artefacts avant de reconstruire&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Vêtements, fourrure, détail de matière&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;True Texture&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Optimisé micro-texture, accepte l'hallucination&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Portrait, réalisme critique&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Natural HD&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Échoue avec élégance, pas de peau cireuse&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Animation, stylisé, social&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Cinema Vivid&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Impact couleur plutôt que fidélité de résolution&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Historique de dégradation inconnu&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Clear Reality&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Meilleur comportement dans le pire cas&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Archive / probatoire&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Natural HD, réglages doux&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;N'inventez pas un détail que vous ne pouvez défendre&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  La règle du 2× que personne ne mentionne
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Doubler deux fois de suite (360p → 720p → 1440p) donne presque toujours un meilleur résultat que sauter directement à 4×, pour deux raisons : chaque étape a moins de marge pour halluciner, et vous obtenez un point de contrôle pour inspecter avant de vous engager.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Le coût est le temps. Le bénéfice est que quand la première étape se passe mal, vous le découvrez &lt;strong&gt;avant&lt;/strong&gt; d'avoir cuit l'erreur dans un fichier 4K qu'il faut ensuite refaire.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Ce que la 4K vous achète réellement
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Si votre source est en 360p, une sortie 4K n'est pas de la « qualité 4K » — c'est une image 360p dans un conteneur aux dimensions 4K. Ce que vous obtenez :&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Moins d'artefacts de compression visibles&lt;/strong&gt; à distance normale (le principal bénéfice réel)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Une netteté perçue supérieure&lt;/strong&gt; si le preset correspondait au contenu&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Aucune information nouvelle.&lt;/strong&gt; Le détail qui n'a jamais été capturé ne se récupère pas, il s'invente de façon plausible.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Ce dernier point sépare l'upscale utile de la déception. Fixez l'attente à « plus propre et plus présentable », pas à « restauré en 4K natif », et les résultats cessent de ressembler à une arnaque.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;p&gt;Si vous voulez essayer les presets sur vos propres images sans rien installer, ils tournent dans le navigateur sur &lt;a href="https://upgolab.com/fr/upscale" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;upgolab.com&lt;/a&gt; — offre gratuite incluse. Les images ci-dessus sont de vraies sorties de preset, pas des rendus marketing.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Si cela vous a été utile, la suite qui vaut la lecture est &lt;em&gt;pourquoi la cohérence temporelle, et non la résolution, est le vrai goulot d'étranglement de l'upscale vidéo&lt;/em&gt; — même chaîne, et cela explique pourquoi une image qui semble parfaite peut encore scintiller en mouvement.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;几乎所有说"AI 放大把我的视频搞得更糟"的人，症状判断是对的，但找错了元凶。他们把 360p 的片子丢进 4 倍模型，得到一坨塑料感的 1440p，于是断定放大是智商税。&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;并不是。真实情况是：他们用&lt;strong&gt;一个&lt;/strong&gt;修复模型去处理需要&lt;strong&gt;四种&lt;/strong&gt;不同模型的素材。4K 输出不是一件成品，而是一条链路的最后一步，而链上每个预设都在为不同类型损伤做优化。&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;本文讲我最常用的五个预设、每个在像素层面到底做了什么，以及该选哪个的判断规则。如果只看一样东西，跳到最后的判断表——但推理过程比表格更重要，因为预设之间会互相影响。&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  错误认知：把放大当成单一操作
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;神经网络放大器同时在干两件事：&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;重建（reconstruction）&lt;/strong&gt; —— 在源素材没有细节的地方编出可信的细节（边缘、纹理、发丝）。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;修复（restoration）&lt;/strong&gt; —— 去掉上一道压缩已经焊进去的瑕疵（块效应、振铃、色带、蚊式噪声）。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;这两件事互相打架。如果你对满是 JPEG 块效应的素材猛拉重建，模型会非常自信地把那些块锐化成一个个清晰的小方块。这就是"放大后更糟"现象的真相，是模型选错，不是 4K 的问题。&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;所以真正的问题从来不是&lt;em&gt;"哪个放大器最强"&lt;/em&gt;，而是&lt;strong&gt;"这个文件受的是什么伤，哪个模型最不容易把这种伤放大？"&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  五个预设各自到底在优化什么
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;以下是对照：同一主体、同一源分辨率、同一倍率，只换预设。全部是真实输出，不是营销渲染图。&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Natural HD —— 安全默认项
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Ffiles.catbox.moe%2F1k5ox3.jpg" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Ffiles.catbox.moe%2F1k5ox3.jpg" alt="Natural HD 预设：人像前后对比，左侧柔和原图，右侧细节还原" width="" height=""&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;这个预设最努力做到&lt;strong&gt;不&lt;/strong&gt;像 AI 处理过。它只重建到"在正常观看距离下读起来够清晰"所需的最小细节，然后停手。&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;强项：&lt;/strong&gt; 几乎没有光晕伪影，皮肤不会变成蜡像而是保留肤色，文字仍然可读。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;弱项：&lt;/strong&gt; 它拒绝编造源素材真正丢掉的发丝或织物纹理。需要取证级细节时，它故意给不够。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;用在：&lt;/strong&gt; 一切写实比锐利更重要的场景 —— 人像、产品图、房产、采访视频、家庭照片。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;如果一辈子只用一个预设，用它。&lt;strong&gt;它失败得很温和&lt;/strong&gt;，这一点大多数模型做不到。&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Ultra Crisp —— 给"本来清晰只是发虚"的素材
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Ffiles.catbox.moe%2Fy8lxqy.jpg" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Ffiles.catbox.moe%2Fy8lxqy.jpg" alt="Ultra Crisp 预设：蒸汽朋克 cosplay 人像，放大后边缘与金属配件被还原" width="" height=""&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Ultra Crisp 假定源素材边缘是干净的，只是被模糊了、没被摧毁。它猛烈拉高边缘对比。&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;强项：&lt;/strong&gt; 图形、插画、白底产品图、UI 截图、cosplay 与服装细节、一切主体与背景边界分明的素材。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;弱项：&lt;/strong&gt; 对噪点多或压缩重的素材，它连噪声一起锐化。高对比边缘出现光晕。皮肤会变糙。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;用在：&lt;/strong&gt; 素材是被&lt;strong&gt;缩小&lt;/strong&gt;的，而不是被&lt;strong&gt;压坏&lt;/strong&gt;的。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;这个区别很关键：&lt;strong&gt;缩小&lt;/strong&gt;意味着细节被平均掉了，可以部分还原。&lt;strong&gt;压坏&lt;/strong&gt;意味着细节被压缩瑕疵替代了，猛拉锐化只会让瑕疵更响。&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  True Texture —— 重建织物与材质
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Ffiles.catbox.moe%2Fyom6ix.jpg" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Ffiles.catbox.moe%2Fyom6ix.jpg" alt="True Texture 预设：冬季外套与仿毛领，右半侧材质纹理被还原" width="" height=""&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;True Texture 针对材质表面调校：针织、毛皮、牛仔、皮革、木纹、头发。它优先可信的微观纹理，而不是边缘锐度。&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;强项：&lt;/strong&gt; 衣服和表面不再像涂了漆的塑料。毛皮和针织在 100% 放大下看起来是对的。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;弱项：&lt;/strong&gt; 它可能编出从未存在过的纹理，这对需要准确性的人（医疗、档案、证据材料）是问题。而且更慢。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;用在：&lt;/strong&gt; 时尚、能看到服装细节的人像、想让材质有真实感的旧照片修复。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;关于 True Texture 必须理解一点：它是&lt;strong&gt;最愿意幻觉&lt;/strong&gt;的预设。做营销图是优点，做任何需要举证的用途是负资产。&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Cinema Vivid —— 改的是色彩对比，不是分辨率
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Ffiles.catbox.moe%2Fccu1ds.jpg" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Ffiles.catbox.moe%2Fccu1ds.jpg" alt="Cinema Vivid 预设：动漫插画，左半侧暗淡，右半侧高饱和高对比" width="" height=""&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Cinema Vivid 几乎不碰分辨率。它改的是色调映射 —— 饱和度、局部对比、黑场。&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;强项：&lt;/strong&gt; 平淡、发灰、类似 Log 拍摄或调色不到位的素材会活过来。适合动画和风格化内容，因为这类素材本来就靠色彩分离取胜。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;弱项：&lt;/strong&gt; 本来饱和度就高的素材会被推到溢出。肤色会往橙里跑。&lt;strong&gt;它根本不是修复型预设。&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;用在：&lt;/strong&gt; 社交内容、动画、封面图 —— 一切"冲击力"胜过"准确性"的场景。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;这个要对自己诚实。它是披着放大器外衣的&lt;strong&gt;调色&lt;/strong&gt;。知道这点就没问题。&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Clear Reality —— 现实混合损伤的全能项
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Ffiles.catbox.moe%2F09rq4n.jpg" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Ffiles.catbox.moe%2F09rq4n.jpg" alt="Clear Reality 预设：户外人像，虚化的背景结构被还原，主体保持自然" width="" height=""&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Clear Reality 试图在重建和压制瑕疵之间取平衡。&lt;strong&gt;不知道素材来历&lt;/strong&gt;时我用它 —— 来源不明的手机视频、下载的片段、截图的截图。&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;强项：&lt;/strong&gt; 处理混合损伤（一点虚、一点压缩、一点噪声），任何方向都不至于翻车。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;弱项：&lt;/strong&gt; 它是折中项，所以单项几乎从不是最好的。素材干净时 Ultra Crisp 更强；布料上 True Texture 更强。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;用在：&lt;/strong&gt; 无法逐帧检查的、异质的真实素材。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  为什么顺序比预设更重要
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;这是几乎所有教程都跳过的一段。&lt;strong&gt;选预设是第二个决定。第一个决定是放大器跑之前你做了什么。&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;如果源素材有明显块效应或蚊式噪声，&lt;strong&gt;先&lt;/strong&gt;降噪。如果先放大再降噪，放大器已经把瑕疵放大成了高对比细节，降噪器现在要跟自家模型的输出打架。你亏两次。&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;实际有效的顺序：&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;检查&lt;/strong&gt; —— 放大到 200~400%。判断主导损伤：虚化、块效应、噪声、还是色带。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;降噪&lt;/strong&gt; —— 有块效应或噪声时做。轻手。目标是去瑕疵，不是去细节。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;校正色彩/曝光&lt;/strong&gt; —— 在放大&lt;strong&gt;之前&lt;/strong&gt;，不是之后。把过曝的帧拿去放大，等于把死白焊死。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;放大&lt;/strong&gt; —— 用匹配&lt;strong&gt;内容类型&lt;/strong&gt;的预设（见下表）。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;最后锐化&lt;/strong&gt;，且轻。放大后一点轻量的 USM 可以找回观感锐度，而不重新引入光晕。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  判断表
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;源素材状态&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;预设&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;原因&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;干净但尺寸小（被缩小）&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Ultra Crisp&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;边缘完好，只是被平均 —— 可还原&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;块效应 / 蚊式噪声&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;先降噪 → Clear Reality&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;重建前先压住瑕疵&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;衣服、毛皮、材质细节&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;True Texture&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;为微观纹理优化，接受幻觉&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;人像、写实优先&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Natural HD&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;失败温和，皮肤不会蜡化&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;动画、风格化、社交&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Cinema Vivid&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;色彩冲击胜过分辨率保真&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;损伤来历不明&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Clear Reality&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;最坏情况下表现最好&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;档案 / 证据材料&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Natural HD，弱参数&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;不要编造你无法辩护的细节&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  没人提的"两次 2 倍"法则
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;连续倍两次（360p → 720p → 1440p）几乎总比一步到 4 倍好，两个原因：每步幻觉空间更小，而且你有检查点可以先看再定。&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;代价是时间。收益是：第一步做错时，你在把错误焊进 4K 文件、之后不得不重做&lt;strong&gt;之前&lt;/strong&gt;就发现了。&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  4K 到底买到了什么
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;源素材是 360p 的话，4K 输出不是"4K 画质" —— 是 360p 的画面套上 4K 的容器尺寸。你得到的是：&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;正常观看距离下&lt;strong&gt;压缩瑕疵变少&lt;/strong&gt;（这才是真正的最大收益）&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;预设匹配内容时&lt;strong&gt;观感锐度提升&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;零新信息&lt;/strong&gt;。没被拍到的细节无法还原，只能被可信地编造。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;最后这点是"有用的放大"和"失望"之间的分界线。把预期定在"更干净、更拿得出手"，而不是"还原成原生 4K"，结果就不再像智商税了。&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;p&gt;想拿自己的素材试这些预设，不用装任何东西，浏览器里就能跑 → &lt;a href="https://upgolab.com/zh/upscale" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;upgolab.com&lt;/a&gt;，有免费额度。上面的图是真实预设输出，不是营销渲染。&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;如果这篇有用，下一篇值得读的是"每一帧都清晰，视频却在抖" —— 讲时间一致性，解释为什么静帧看着完美的画面一动就崩。&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A typical social media holiday calendar lists 150 days a month: Talk Like a Pirate Day, National Cheeseburger Day, World Beard Day. That works for a brand with a designer and a content team. A founder posting between support tickets and a deploy needs the opposite: the handful of dates in the last quarter of 2026 that actually connect to what you build, and permission to ignore the rest.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is that shorter list. Eight dates or windows between now and early January, each with what to post and when to schedule it. Every date below was checked against its organizer or a published calendar on September 25, 2026.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Why a short holiday calendar beats a long one
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A holiday post only works when the reader can see why &lt;em&gt;you&lt;/em&gt; are posting about it. A developer tool posting about National Guacamole Day reads as filler, and filler is what people scroll past. A post about your year of shipping, published the week everyone is looking back, reads as timely.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The other reason is time. Each date you commit to is a post to write, adjust per network and schedule. Eight is a number you can prepare in one sitting in October and then stop thinking about.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  1. Dates only your company has
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Start with the calendar nobody else can copy: the day you launched, the day you shipped the feature people ask about most, the day your first paying customer signed up, the anniversary of going full-time. Write down the ones that fall between October and December.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;These make the strongest posts on the list because they are true, specific and yours. "One year ago today we shipped v1. Here is what changed since" gives a reader something a generic holiday never can. Use real numbers only if you are happy to share them; a post about what you learned needs none.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  2. The clock change: October 25 and November 1
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Not a holiday, but the date on this list most likely to break your schedule. Clocks go back one hour in the UK and the EU on &lt;a href="https://www.timeanddate.com/time/change/uk/london" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Sunday, October 25, 2026&lt;/a&gt;, and in the US and Canada on &lt;a href="https://www.timeanddate.com/time/change/usa/new-york" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Sunday, November 1, 2026&lt;/a&gt;. For the week in between, the gap between London and New York is four hours instead of five.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you picked your posting slots for a US audience while living in Europe, or the other way round, check which clock each slot follows before that week. A LinkedIn post meant for 8:30 in New York can land at 7:30 instead, before most of your readers are at their desks.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  3. Hacktoberfest: all of October
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For developer-founders, October means &lt;a href="https://hacktoberfest.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Hacktoberfest&lt;/a&gt;, presented by DigitalOcean and run with MLH and DEV. The 2026 edition moved away from counting pull requests: it is built around in-person and online events, called Fests, about building with open-source AI.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If your product is open source or has an open-source part, this is the month to post a "good first issue" list, a thank-you to contributors, or a write-up of a Fest you attended or hosted. Long versions belong on DEV, where the event's community already reads; shorter cuts fit Bluesky and Mastodon, where developers spend a lot of their time.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  4. Global Entrepreneurship Week: November 16 to 22
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.genglobal.org/gew" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Global Entrepreneurship Week&lt;/a&gt; runs from Monday, November 16 to Sunday, November 22, 2026, according to its organizer, the Global Entrepreneurship Network. It is the one week of the year when "founder story" posts match what everyone else is talking about.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Use it for the posts you keep postponing: why you started, the mistake that cost you a month, the tool you stopped paying for. One post a day for the week is realistic if you write all seven in one go beforehand. LinkedIn is the natural home; Threads takes a shorter, more casual version of the same story.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  5. Black Friday to Cyber Monday: November 27 to 30
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;US Thanksgiving is Thursday, November 26, so Black Friday is November 27, &lt;a href="https://www.sba.gov/about-sba/organization/observances/small-business-saturday/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Small Business Saturday&lt;/a&gt; is November 28, and Cyber Monday is November 30. If you sell a product with a price, this is the weekend people expect a deal, and the one where feeds are most crowded.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you run an offer, it needs a sequence, not one post: an announcement, a reminder halfway through, and a "last hours" post before it ends, each with the exact end time and time zone. Write all of them at once and schedule them together. In Clienzo you can put one post into several time slots in a single step, which suits exactly this kind of short run (&lt;a href="https://clienzo.co/features/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;see the scheduling features&lt;/a&gt;). If you are not running a deal, say that in one post; "No Black Friday sale, our prices stay the same all year" is a clear position that some buyers respect.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  6. GivingTuesday: December 1
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.givingtuesday.org/participate/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;GivingTuesday&lt;/a&gt; falls on Tuesday, December 1, 2026, the Tuesday after US Thanksgiving. Post about it only if you actually give something: you sponsor the open-source libraries your product runs on, you offer free accounts to nonprofits, or you donate part of a month's revenue.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you do, name what and to whom, with a link. A post that says "we sponsor the three libraries our app could not exist without" is useful to other founders and credits the maintainers. A post that just uses the hashtag without any giving behind it is the kind readers notice.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  7. The year-end recap: December 14 to 23
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The weeks before the holidays are when year-in-review posts get read. After about December 23, many of your readers are offline until the new year, and so, ideally, are you. Publish your recap before that window closes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A founder's recap does not need a revenue chart. What you shipped, what you dropped, what you would do differently and what comes next all make good material. Write the long version once, then cut it per network: a full article on DEV or LinkedIn, a short thread-length version on Threads and Bluesky, a single photo with a caption on Instagram. If you post to Instagram, remember it now caps a post at five hashtags (&lt;a href="https://clienzo.co/blog/instagram-updates-2026-founders/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;more on this year's Instagram changes&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  8. The first Monday back: January 4, 2027
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Monday, January 4, 2027 is the first full working day of the year for most of your audience. Prepare it in December, when you still remember the year in detail: a "what we are building in Q1" post, a changelog of what shipped over the break, or a question to your followers about what they want next.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Schedule it before you log off for the holidays. That way your account restarts on the day your readers do, not three days later when you finally clear your inbox.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  How to prepare the whole quarter in one sitting
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Eight dates sounds like eight interruptions. It is one afternoon if you batch it. Block two hours in the first week of October and work through them in this order:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Put every date in your calendar first&lt;/strong&gt;, including your own company dates from item 1, so you can see the gaps and the clusters (late November stacks four days together)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Write the main version of each post&lt;/strong&gt; for the network where your audience is largest, before thinking about any other network&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Cut each one down per network&lt;/strong&gt;: Bluesky stops at 300 characters, Threads at 500, and a LinkedIn post can run much longer, so the same idea needs a different length on each&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Pick the images once&lt;/strong&gt; and reuse them; a single cover for the year-end recap can serve every network it goes to&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Schedule everything, then check the week of the clock change&lt;/strong&gt; separately, since that is where a correct slot most often turns into a wrong one&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Leave room for what you cannot plan: a release that slips, a customer question worth answering in public. A calendar with eight fixed posts in three months still leaves most days free for those.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  The dates to skip
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Most of a long social media holiday calendar is safe to ignore. Leave these out unless your product has a direct link to them:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Food and fun days (Cheeseburger Day, Talk Like a Pirate Day, Batman Day): fine for a restaurant, filler for a software product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Awareness days you have no stake in: a post that borrows a cause only for reach reads as exactly that&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Halloween and seasonal jokes, unless making them is already part of how your account sounds&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Every regional holiday outside the markets your customers are in&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A good test: if you would not mention the day to a customer on a call, do not post about it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  The short version
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Your own dates first: launch day, big releases, first customer, going full-time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;October 25 and November 1: check which clock your posting slots follow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;October: Hacktoberfest posts if you build in the open, long on DEV, short on Bluesky and Mastodon&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;November 16 to 22: Global Entrepreneurship Week, a week of founder stories&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;November 27 to 30: a scheduled sequence if you run a deal, one clear post if you do not&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;December 1: GivingTuesday, only if you actually give&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;December 14 to 23: publish your year-end recap before readers go offline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;January 4, 2027: have your first post of the year scheduled before the break&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Put all eight in your calendar this week, write the posts in one session in October, and schedule them. The quarter then runs without you having to remember any of it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Related reading
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://clienzo.co/blog/social-media-goals-solo-founder/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Social media goals you can measure when you post alone&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://clienzo.co/blog/best-time-to-post-social-media-studies-compared/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;What three studies say about the best time to post&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://clienzo.co/blog/text-snippets-social-media-founders/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Eight text snippets worth saving once and reusing&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Originally published on the &lt;a href="https://clienzo.co/blog/social-media-holiday-calendar-q4-2026-founders/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Clienzo blog&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;"AI로 4K 만들었더니 원본보다 더 나빠졌다" — 이 말은 틀리지 않았습니다. 다만 범인은 4K가 아닙니다. 범인은 &lt;strong&gt;손상 유형에 맞지 않는 프리셋을 고른 것&lt;/strong&gt;입니다.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;360p 영상을 4배 모델에 넣고 뭉개진 1440p를 받은 다음 "업스케일은 사기다"라고 결론짓습니다. 기분은 이해하지만, 실제로 일어난 일은 다른 것입니다.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  업스케일은 "하나의 작업"이 아닙니다
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;뉴럴 업스케일러는 동시에 두 가지 일을 합니다.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;재구성(reconstruction)&lt;/strong&gt; — 원본에 없는 디테일을 그럴듯하게 만들어냅니다. 윤곽, 텍스처, 머리카락 한 올.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;복원(restoration)&lt;/strong&gt; — 앞단 압축이 이미 구워 넣은 아티팩트를 제거합니다. 블록 노이즈, 링잉, 밴딩, 모스키토 노이즈.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;문제는 &lt;strong&gt;이 두 작업이 서로 방해한다는 것&lt;/strong&gt;입니다. 블록 노이즈투성이 원본에 재구성을 강하게 걸면, 모델은 그 블록을 "선명한 작은 사각형"으로 자신 있게 강조합니다. 이것이 "업스케일하면 나빠진다" 현상의 정체이고, 모델 선택의 실수이지 4K의 문제가 아닙니다.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;그래서 진짜 질문은 &lt;em&gt;"어떤 업스케일러가 최고인가"&lt;/em&gt; 가 아니라 &lt;strong&gt;"이 파일은 어떤 손상을 입었고, 어떤 모델이 그 손상을 증폭시키지 않는가"&lt;/strong&gt; 입니다.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  5개 프리셋이 실제로 최적화하는 것
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;아래는 같은 피사체, 같은 원본 해상도, 같은 배율에서 프리셋만 바꾼 비교입니다. 모두 실제 출력이며 마케팅용 렌더가 아닙니다.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Natural HD — 안전한 기본값
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Ffiles.catbox.moe%2F1k5ox3.jpg" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Ffiles.catbox.moe%2F1k5ox3.jpg" alt="Natural HD 프리셋: 인물 사진 비포/애프터. 왼쪽은 부드러운 원본, 오른쪽은 복원된 디테일" width="" height=""&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;"AI 티가 나지 않는 것"을 가장 우선하는 프리셋입니다. 일반적인 시청 거리에서 선명하게 읽히는 최소한의 디테일만 재구성하고 멈춥니다.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;강점:&lt;/strong&gt; 헤일로 아티팩트가 거의 없음. 피부가 밀랍처럼 되지 않고 피부색을 유지. 텍스트가 읽힘.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;약점:&lt;/strong&gt; 원본에서 진짜로 사라진 머리카락 결이나 직물 짜임을 의도적으로 만들지 않음. 포렌식 수준 디테일이 필요한 용도에는 부족.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;쓸 곳:&lt;/strong&gt; 사실감이 선명도보다 중요한 모든 것 — 인물, 제품 사진, 부동산, 인터뷰 영상, 가족 사진.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;평생 프리셋 하나만 쓴다면 이걸 쓰세요. &lt;strong&gt;실패하는 방식이 온화&lt;/strong&gt;한데, 이는 대부분의 모델이 못 하는 장점입니다.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Ultra Crisp — "선명했는데 흐릿해진" 콘텐츠용
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Ffiles.catbox.moe%2Fy8lxqy.jpg" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Ffiles.catbox.moe%2Fy8lxqy.jpg" alt="Ultra Crisp 프리셋: 스팀펑크 코스프레 인물. 업스케일 후 윤곽과 금속 장식이 복원됨" width="" height=""&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Ultra Crisp은 원본의 윤곽이 "파괴되지 않고 단지 블러 처리되었다"고 가정하고, 에지 대비를 공격적으로 올립니다.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;강점:&lt;/strong&gt; 그래픽, 일러스트, 흰 배경 제품컷, UI 스크린샷, 코스프레·의상 디테일, 피사체와 배경 경계가 뚜렷한 모든 것에서 우수.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;약점:&lt;/strong&gt; 노이즈가 많거나 심하게 압축된 원본에서는 노이즈까지 선명하게 만듭니다. 고대비 윤곽에 헤일로가 생김. 피부가 거칠어짐.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;쓸 곳:&lt;/strong&gt; 원본이 &lt;strong&gt;축소&lt;/strong&gt;된 것이지 &lt;strong&gt;심하게 압축&lt;/strong&gt;된 것이 아닌 경우.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;이 구분이 중요합니다. &lt;strong&gt;축소&lt;/strong&gt;는 디테일이 평균화되어 사라진 상태로 일부 복원 가능합니다. &lt;strong&gt;심한 압축&lt;/strong&gt;은 디테일이 압축 아티팩트로 대체된 상태로, 강하게 선명화하면 아티팩트만 더 시끄러워집니다.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  True Texture — 직물과 소재 재구성
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Ffiles.catbox.moe%2Fyom6ix.jpg" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Ffiles.catbox.moe%2Fyom6ix.jpg" alt="True Texture 프리셋: 겨울 코트와 인조 퍼. 오른쪽 절반에서 소재 텍스처가 복원됨" width="" height=""&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;니트, 퍼, 데님, 가죽, 나뭇결, 머리카락 등 &lt;strong&gt;소재 표면&lt;/strong&gt;에 맞춰 조정된 프리셋입니다. 에지 선명도보다 그럴듯한 미세 텍스처를 우선합니다.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;강점:&lt;/strong&gt; 옷과 표면이 "칠한 플라스틱"처럼 보이지 않게 됩니다. 퍼와 니트가 100% 확대에서 제대로 보임.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;약점:&lt;/strong&gt; 원래 없던 텍스처를 만들어낼 수 있으며, 정확성이 필요한 용도(의료, 아카이브, 증거 자료)에서는 문제입니다. 처리도 느립니다.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;쓸 곳:&lt;/strong&gt; 패션, 의상 디테일이 보이는 인물 사진, 소재감을 살리고 싶은 오래된 사진 복원.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;True Texture에 대해 알아야 할 점: &lt;strong&gt;환각을 가장 잘 일으키는&lt;/strong&gt; 프리셋입니다. 마케팅 이미지에는 장점, 증거성이 요구되는 용도에는 부채입니다.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Cinema Vivid — 해상도가 아니라 색과 대비
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Ffiles.catbox.moe%2Fccu1ds.jpg" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Ffiles.catbox.moe%2Fccu1ds.jpg" alt="Cinema Vivid 프리셋: 애니메이션 일러스트. 왼쪽은 칙칙한 색, 오른쪽은 고채도·고대비" width="" height=""&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Cinema Vivid는 해상도를 거의 건드리지 않습니다. 바꾸는 것은 톤 매핑 — 채도, 국소 대비, 블랙 포인트입니다.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;강점:&lt;/strong&gt; 평평하고 칙칙한, Log 촬영 같거나 색보정이 아쉬운 영상이 살아납니다. 색 분리가 핵심인 애니메이션과 양식화된 콘텐츠에 잘 맞음.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;약점:&lt;/strong&gt; 이미 채도가 높은 소재는 클리핑까지 밀어붙입니다. 피부톤이 주황으로 흐름. &lt;strong&gt;애초에 복원 프리셋이 아닙니다.&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;쓸 곳:&lt;/strong&gt; SNS용, 애니메이션, 썸네일 — "정확성"보다 "임팩트"가 필요한 것.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;이건 솔직해집시다. 업스케일러 옷을 입은 &lt;strong&gt;색보정&lt;/strong&gt;입니다. 그걸 알고 쓰면 문제없습니다.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Clear Reality — 실제 세계 복합 손상용 올라운더
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Ffiles.catbox.moe%2F09rq4n.jpg" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Ffiles.catbox.moe%2F09rq4n.jpg" alt="Clear Reality 프리셋: 야외 인물 사진. 흐릿했던 배경 구조가 복원되고 피사체는 자연스럽게 유지됨" width="" height=""&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;재구성과 아티팩트 억제의 균형을 잡으려는 프리셋입니다. &lt;strong&gt;원본의 이력을 모를 때&lt;/strong&gt; 사용합니다 — 출처 불명의 스마트폰 영상, 다운로드한 클립, 스크린샷의 스크린샷.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;강점:&lt;/strong&gt; 복합 손상(약간의 블러, 약간의 압축, 약간의 노이즈)을 어느 방향으로도 극적으로 실패하지 않고 처리.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;약점:&lt;/strong&gt; 절충안이라 단일 항목에서 최고가 되기는 드뭅니다. 깨끗한 소재에는 Ultra Crisp이 낫고, 직물에는 True Texture가 낫습니다.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;쓸 곳:&lt;/strong&gt; 모든 프레임을 검사할 수 없는 이질적인 실제 영상.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  왜 "순서"가 프리셋 선택보다 중요한가
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;대부분의 튜토리얼이 건너뛰는 부분입니다. &lt;strong&gt;프리셋 선택은 두 번째 결정입니다. 첫 번째 결정은 업스케일러를 돌리기 전에 무엇을 하느냐입니다.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;원본에 눈에 보이는 블록 노이즈나 모스키토 노이즈가 있으면 &lt;strong&gt;먼저&lt;/strong&gt; 디노이즈를 거세요. 먼저 업스케일하고 나중에 디노이즈하면, 업스케일러가 이미 아티팩트를 고대비 디테일로 증폭해버려서 디노이저가 자기 모델의 출력과 싸워야 합니다. 두 번 손해입니다.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;실제로 작동하는 순서:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;검사&lt;/strong&gt; — 200~400% 확대. 지배적인 손상을 파악: 블러, 블록, 노이즈, 밴딩 중 무엇인지.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;디노이즈&lt;/strong&gt; — 블록이나 노이즈가 있으면. 약하게. 아티팩트를 없애는 것이지 디테일을 없애는 게 아닙니다.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;색·노출 보정&lt;/strong&gt; — 업스케일 &lt;strong&gt;전&lt;/strong&gt;에. 노출 오버된 프레임을 업스케일하면 화이트 클리핑이 구워집니다.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;업스케일&lt;/strong&gt; — &lt;strong&gt;콘텐츠 유형&lt;/strong&gt;에 맞춘 프리셋으로 (아래 표).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;선명화는 마지막&lt;/strong&gt;, 약하게. 업스케일 후 가벼운 언샤프 마스크는 헤일로를 재도입하지 않고 체감 선명도를 회복합니다.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  판단 표
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;원본 상태&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;프리셋&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;이유&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;깨끗하지만 작음 (축소됨)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Ultra Crisp&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;윤곽은 무사, 평균화만 됨 = 복원 가능&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;블록·모스키토 노이즈&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;디노이즈 → Clear Reality&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;재구성 전에 아티팩트 억제&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;옷·퍼·소재 디테일&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;True Texture&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;미세 텍스처에 최적화, 환각 허용&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;인물·사실감 중시&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Natural HD&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;실패가 온화, 피부가 밀랍처럼 되지 않음&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;애니·양식화·SNS&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Cinema Vivid&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;해상도보다 색 임팩트&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;손상 이력 불명&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Clear Reality&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;최악의 경우에 최선의 동작&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;아카이브·증거 자료&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Natural HD, 약한 설정&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;방어할 수 없는 디테일을 만들지 않음&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  아무도 말하지 않는 "2배 법칙"
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;두 번에 나눠 배로 만드는 것(360p → 720p → 1440p)이 한 번에 4배 하는 것보다 거의 항상 좋습니다. 이유는 두 가지: 각 단계에서 환각의 여지가 작고, 커밋하기 전에 확인할 체크포인트가 생깁니다.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;비용은 시간입니다. 이득은 1단계가 잘못됐을 때, 그 오류를 4K 파일에 구워 넣은 &lt;strong&gt;후&lt;/strong&gt;가 아니라 &lt;strong&gt;전&lt;/strong&gt;에 알 수 있다는 것입니다.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  4K가 실제로 주는 것
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;원본이 360p라면, 4K 출력은 "4K 화질"이 아닙니다 — 360p 이미지에 4K 컨테이너 치수를 준 것입니다. 얻는 것은:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;일반 시청 거리에서 &lt;strong&gt;압축 아티팩트 감소&lt;/strong&gt; (실질적 최대 이득)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;프리셋이 소재에 맞았다면 &lt;strong&gt;체감 선명도 향상&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;새로운 정보는 0&lt;/strong&gt;. 촬영되지 않은 디테일은 복원되지 않고 그럴듯하게 날조될 뿐입니다.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;이 마지막 점이 유용한 업스케일과 실망을 가릅니다. 기대치를 "더 깨끗하고 보기 좋게"로 잡고 "네이티브 4K로 복원"이라고 생각하지 않으면, 결과가 사기처럼 느껴지지 않습니다.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;p&gt;가지고 있는 소재로 프리셋을 시험해보고 싶다면, 설치 없이 브라우저에서 돌아갑니다 → &lt;a href="https://upgolab.com/ko/upscale" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;upgolab.com&lt;/a&gt;. 무료 플랜이 있습니다. 위 이미지는 실제 프리셋 출력이며 마케팅 렌더가 아닙니다.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;계속 읽을 만한 다음 글은 "프레임은 선명한데 영상이 떨리는 이유" — 시간적 일관성 이야기로, 정지 화면에서 완벽해 보이는 프레임이 움직임 속에서 왜 무너지는지 설명합니다.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Traditional AI chat interfaces (like ChatGPT, Claude, and Gemini) have a fundamental UX flaw: everything flows to the bottom.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If an LLM writes a 600-word response and you have a doubt about a sentence at the top, you are forced to scroll to the very bottom, manually re-quote the text, and ask your question—completely breaking your reading flow.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;To solve this, I built @zefina/inline-discussions: an open-source React engine that brings Google Docs-style contextual threads directly inside AI Markdown responses.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;1) Video Demo:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;a href="https://dev.tourl"&gt;https://www.linkedin.com/posts/jagath-saradagi-a3924035b_ai-uxdesign-generativeai-ugcPost-7483515162319323136-_B7o&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;2)Live Interactive &lt;a href="https://dev.tourl"&gt;Playground:https://jagathsaradagi.github.io/inline-discussions/&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;3)GitHub Repository:&lt;a href="https://dev.tourl"&gt;https://github.com/JagathSaradagi/inline-discussions&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;How It Works&lt;br&gt;
Highlight Any Sentence: Select any text in an AI response to open an in-situ ask box directly beneath that sentence.&lt;br&gt;
DOM-to-AST Source Mapping: The engine maps browser text selections back to raw Markdown source coordinates using AST character maps.&lt;br&gt;
Sibling-Block AST Injection: Instead of illegally nesting &lt;/p&gt; cards inside HTML &lt;p&gt; tags, the compiler splits the parent paragraph into valid sibling blocks.&lt;br&gt;
Arbitrary Recursion: You can highlight text inside a nested clarification at Depth 1 to branch a Depth 2 discussion, creating structured conversation trees.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The engine is completely headless, works with any AI model or backend, and is AGPL-3.0 dual-licensed.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Check out the interactive playground and let me know your thoughts!&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Quase todo mundo que diz "o upscale com IA piorou meu vídeo" está certo sobre o sintoma e errado sobre o culpado. Passaram um clipe de 360p por um modelo 4×, receberam um arquivo 1440p com cara de plástico, e concluíram que upscale é golpe.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Não é. O que aconteceu é que aplicaram &lt;strong&gt;um único&lt;/strong&gt; modelo de restauração a um conteúdo que precisava de &lt;strong&gt;quatro&lt;/strong&gt; diferentes. Uma saída em 4K não é um produto; é o último passo de uma cadeia, e cada preset dessa cadeia otimiza para um tipo de dano diferente.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Este artigo passa pelos cinco presets que mais uso, o que cada um faz no nível do pixel, e as regras de decisão para saber qual escolher. Se for ler só uma coisa, pule para a tabela no final — mas o raciocínio importa mais que a tabela, porque os presets interagem.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  O erro: tratar upscale como uma operação só
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Um upscaler neural faz dois trabalhos ao mesmo tempo:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Reconstrução&lt;/strong&gt; — inventa detalhe plausível onde a fonte não tem (bordas, textura, fios de cabelo).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Restauração&lt;/strong&gt; — remove os artefatos que a compressão anterior já assou (blocos, ringing, banding, ruído de mosquito).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Esses dois trabalhos brigam entre si. Se você empurra a reconstrução com força numa fonte cheia de blocos de JPEG, o modelo afia os blocos com toda confiança até virarem retângulos nítidos. Esse é o fenômeno do "piorou depois do upscale", e é erro de escolha de modelo, não problema do 4K.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Então a pergunta real nunca é &lt;em&gt;"qual é o melhor upscaler?"&lt;/em&gt; — é &lt;strong&gt;"que tipo de dano esse arquivo específico tem, e qual modelo é menos propenso a amplificar esse dano?"&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  O que cada preset realmente otimiza
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Estes são os cinco que mantenho em rotação, com uma descrição honesta do trade-off de cada um. Todos os exemplos são o mesmo sujeito, a mesma resolução de origem e o mesmo fator de escala — só o preset muda.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Natural HD — o valor seguro
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Ffiles.catbox.moe%2F1k5ox3.jpg" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Ffiles.catbox.moe%2F1k5ox3.jpg" alt="Preset Natural HD: comparação antes/depois em um retrato, fonte suave à esquerda, detalhe resolvido à direita" width="" height=""&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;É o preset que mais se esforça para &lt;strong&gt;não&lt;/strong&gt; parecer processado por IA. Reconstrói o detalhe mínimo necessário para a imagem se ler como nítida a distância normal de visualização, e para aí.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Forte em:&lt;/strong&gt; quase nenhum artefato de halo, a pele continua com cor de pele em vez de virar cerosa, o texto continua legível.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Fraco em:&lt;/strong&gt; se recusa a inventar fios de cabelo ou a trama de um tecido que a fonte perdeu de verdade. Se você precisa de detalhe forense, entrega menos de propósito.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Use para:&lt;/strong&gt; tudo onde realismo importa mais que nitidez — retratos, fotos de produto, imobiliário, entrevistas, fotos de família.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Se você só for usar um preset na vida, use este. &lt;strong&gt;Falha com elegância&lt;/strong&gt;, o que é mais do que quase todo modelo pode dizer.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Ultra Crisp — para conteúdo que era nítido mas está mole
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Ffiles.catbox.moe%2Fy8lxqy.jpg" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Ffiles.catbox.moe%2Fy8lxqy.jpg" alt="Preset Ultra Crisp: retrato cosplay steampunk, bordas e ferragens metálicas resolvidas após o upscale" width="" height=""&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Ultra Crisp assume que a fonte tem bordas limpas que foram apenas desfocadas, não destruídas. Empurra o contraste de borda com agressividade.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Forte em:&lt;/strong&gt; gráficos, ilustrações, produto em fundo branco, capturas de UI, detalhe de cosplay e figurino, tudo com fronteiras duras entre sujeito e fundo.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Fraco em:&lt;/strong&gt; em fontes ruidosas ou muito comprimidas, afia o ruído também. Halos aparecem em bordas de alto contraste. A pele pode ficar áspera.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Use para:&lt;/strong&gt; conteúdo que foi &lt;strong&gt;reduzido&lt;/strong&gt; em vez de &lt;strong&gt;mal codificado&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A distinção importa: &lt;strong&gt;reduzido&lt;/strong&gt; significa que o detalhe foi promediado e pode ser parcialmente recuperado. &lt;strong&gt;Mal codificado&lt;/strong&gt; significa que o detalhe foi substituído por artefatos de compressão, e afiar com força só deixa esses artefatos mais altos.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  True Texture — reconstruir tecido e material
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Ffiles.catbox.moe%2Fyom6ix.jpg" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Ffiles.catbox.moe%2Fyom6ix.jpg" alt="Preset True Texture: casaco de inverno e barra de pele sintética, textura do material recuperada na metade direita" width="" height=""&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;True Texture é afinado para superfícies de material: tricô, pele, denim, couro, veio de madeira, cabelo. Prioriza microtextura plausível acima da nitidez de borda.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Forte em:&lt;/strong&gt; roupas e superfícies param de parecer plástico pintado. Pele sintética e tricô se leem corretamente a 100% de zoom.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Fraco em:&lt;/strong&gt; pode inventar textura que nunca existiu, o que é problema se você precisa de exatidão (médico, arquivo, evidência documental). Também é mais lento.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Use para:&lt;/strong&gt; moda, retratos com detalhe visível de roupa, restauração de foto antiga onde você quer que o material pareça real.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;O que precisa entender sobre True Texture: é o preset &lt;strong&gt;mais disposto a alucinar&lt;/strong&gt;. Isso é vantagem para imagem comercial e passivo para qualquer coisa probatória.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Cinema Vivid — cor e contraste, não resolução
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Ffiles.catbox.moe%2Fccu1ds.jpg" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Ffiles.catbox.moe%2Fccu1ds.jpg" alt="Preset Cinema Vivid: ilustração anime, metade esquerda apagada contra metade direita saturada e de alto contraste" width="" height=""&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Cinema Vivid quase não mexe na resolução. O que muda é o mapeamento tonal — saturação, contraste local, ponto de preto.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Forte em:&lt;/strong&gt; material plano, apagado, tipo log ou mal graduado ganha vida. Funciona bem em animação e conteúdo estilizado onde a separação de cor é o objetivo.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Fraco em:&lt;/strong&gt; empurra uma fonte já saturada até o clipping. Tons de pele puxam para laranja. &lt;strong&gt;Não é um preset de restauração de jeito nenhum.&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Use para:&lt;/strong&gt; conteúdo social, animação, thumbnails — tudo onde o &lt;em&gt;impacto&lt;/em&gt; vence a &lt;em&gt;exatidão&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Seja honesto sobre este. É um color grading vestido de upscaler. Tudo bem, desde que você saiba.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Clear Reality — o faz-tudo para dano do mundo real
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Ffiles.catbox.moe%2F09rq4n.jpg" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Ffiles.catbox.moe%2F09rq4n.jpg" alt="Preset Clear Reality: retrato externo, estrutura do fundo desfocado resolvida enquanto o sujeito permanece natural" width="" height=""&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Clear Reality tenta equilibrar reconstrução e supressão de artefatos. É o que uso quando &lt;strong&gt;não conheço a história da fonte&lt;/strong&gt; — vídeo de celular de procedência desconhecida, clipes baixados, captura de captura.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Forte em:&lt;/strong&gt; lida com dano misto (um pouco de desfoque, um pouco de compressão, um pouco de ruído) sem falhar de forma espetacular em nenhuma direção.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Fraco em:&lt;/strong&gt; é a opção de compromisso, então raramente é o &lt;em&gt;melhor&lt;/em&gt; em algo isolado. Em fonte limpa, Ultra Crisp ganha. Em tecido, True Texture ganha.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Use para:&lt;/strong&gt; metragem heterogênea do mundo real onde você não consegue inspecionar cada frame.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Por que a ordem importa mais que o preset
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Esta é a parte que quase todo tutorial pula. &lt;strong&gt;A escolha do preset é a segunda decisão. A primeira é o que acontece antes do upscaler rodar.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Se a sua fonte tem blocos visíveis ou ruído de mosquito, rode uma passada de denoise &lt;strong&gt;antes&lt;/strong&gt;. Se você faz upscale primeiro e denoise depois, o upscaler já amplificou os artefatos em detalhe de alto contraste, e agora o denoiser tem que brigar com a saída do próprio modelo. Você perde duas vezes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A ordem prática que funciona:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Inspecione&lt;/strong&gt; a 200–400% de zoom. Identifique o dano dominante: desfoque, blocos, ruído ou banding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Denoise&lt;/strong&gt; se houver blocos ou ruído. Toque leve — você quer remover artefatos, não detalhe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Corrija cor/exposição&lt;/strong&gt; antes do upscale, não depois. Upscalar um frame superexposto assa o clipping.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Faça upscale&lt;/strong&gt; com o preset casado com o &lt;em&gt;tipo de conteúdo&lt;/em&gt; (tabela abaixo).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Afie no final&lt;/strong&gt;, e com suavidade. Uma máscara de nitidez leve após o upscale recupera nitidez percebida sem reintroduzir halos.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Tabela de decisão
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
